The vendored libzip calls close(), getpid() and friends without declaring them.
<unistd.h> is included only on Apple, and only in mkstemp.c. That was a warning
until C23 made implicit declarations an error, and the build now stops with:

  mkstemp.c: error: implicit declaration of function 'getpid'
  zip_close.c: error: implicit declaration of function 'close'

Two hunks are needed: zipint.h covers the files that include it, and mkstemp.c
does not include zipint.h at all, so its own Apple-only guard is widened.

diff -ur a/core/deps/libzip/mkstemp.c b/core/deps/libzip/mkstemp.c
--- a/core/deps/libzip/mkstemp.c	2026-08-08 18:38:49.745720837 +0100
+++ b/core/deps/libzip/mkstemp.c	2026-08-08 18:41:55.447708593 +0100
@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
 
-#ifdef __APPLE__
+#if defined(__APPLE__) || defined(__unix__)
 #include <unistd.h>
 #endif
 
diff -ur a/core/deps/libzip/zipint.h b/core/deps/libzip/zipint.h
--- a/core/deps/libzip/zipint.h	2026-08-08 18:38:49.746038171 +0100
+++ b/core/deps/libzip/zipint.h	2026-08-08 18:41:55.447676844 +0100
@@ -43,6 +43,12 @@
 #include "zip.h"
 #include "config.h"
 
+#ifndef _WIN32
+/* close(), getpid() and friends. These were used without a declaration,
+   which C23 turned from a warning into an error. */
+#include <unistd.h>
+#endif
+
 #ifndef HAVE_MKSTEMP
 int _zip_mkstemp(char *);
 #define mkstemp _zip_mkstemp
